From 0e643ab3a1ba500932083df1235d0cff863ddd7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amin <roudaky@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:25:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Perf][MRv2] Stage only the uncached prompt suffix of
 prefix-cache hits

Behind VLLM_SUFFIX_STAGING=1 (default off, read once at runner init).

When a new request is added to the V2 model runner, its whole prefill
(token ids, and M-RoPE positions for M-RoPE models) is staged into the
persistent per-request rows RequestState.all_token_ids and
RopeState.prefill_positions via StagedWriteTensor. With a prefix-cache hit
only positions >= num_computed_tokens are ever run, so for workloads with a
long shared cached prefix and a short suffix most of the per-request host
cost (list extend in stage_write, list-to-numpy conversion in copy_to_uva,
list clear in clear_staged_writes, and the H2D write kernel) is spent on
columns that are never read.

With the flag on, a new request with num_computed_tokens > 0 stages only
prefill_token_ids[num_computed_tokens:] at column offset
num_computed_tokens of its row, so every readable column holds exactly
the same value as before and no reader needs an index translation.
The prefill gather and the M-RoPE position gather read from the slot's
GPU num_computed_tokens, which is initialized from num_computed_tokens at
add time and only grows; preemption removes the slot and re-adds the
request as a new request with its full prefill.

The full prompt is still staged when any reader of the prompt columns is
active: per request (penalties, prompt logprobs, thinking budget, and
conservatively bad words, structured outputs, pooling) and runner-wide
(model states other than DefaultModelState / MambaHybridModelState, EVS
multimodal pruning, watermarking, and conservatively speculative
decoding, pooling models, custom logits processors).

Tests (tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_suffix_staging.py): the per-request
predicate and stage start, a pure-Python model showing that staging only
columns >= stage_start at their own offsets preserves every prefill
gather read (query tokens and lookahead) across chunk sizes, and a CUDA
test (skipped without CUDA) that stages a request into a RequestState
slot holding stale data from a previous occupant, runs the real
prepare_prefill_inputs kernel over a chunked prefill, and checks the
gathered input ids and lookahead tokens equal those of full staging.
